##
## cancel_waits — a cancel ends a task's wait at once (jacl_impl#270). A `sleep` waits once, to its
## deadline, and a `read-line` waits on the host's stdin bell until the host rings it, so each ends
## only because the cancel wakes it: the sleep is ten minutes, and stdin has nothing, ever. Prints
## how each task ended.
##

def s [spawn { sleep 600 }]
def r [spawn { read-line }]
sleep 0.02
assert [cancel $s]
assert [cancel $r]
print [error-val [await $s]]
print [error-val [await $r]]
